WEBVTT

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
Kokoro no mori no naka kimi ni deau koto

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
I was always dreaming of meeting you

00:16.130 --> 00:22.180
<b>Zettai Shonen</b>

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
Itsumo yume mitetan da

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
within my heart’s forest.

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
Hikari no silhouette sono saki wo mezashite

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
The silhouette of light guides the way.

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
Itsuka ai ni furete mitai

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
One day, I’d like to try and experience love.

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
Kimochi to kotoba niji to mizutamari

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
My feelings and words can be like rainbows and puddles.

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
Omoiau yasashisa ga michibiku ashita he to

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
The kindness we share will guide us into tomorrow.

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru kara

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
With only you here, I can become stronger.

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
Sora takaku negai wo kanadeyou

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
My wish will be granted in the heights of the sky.

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
Nanika taisetsu ka wo miushinawanu you ni

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
You won’t lose sight of something precious to you,

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
Kitto motto kagayaku kara

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
because I’m sure it’ll shine even brighter.

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru no sa

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
With only you here, I can become stronger.

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Ima dekiru koto kara hajimeyou

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Let’s start with what we can do right now.

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
Mawarimichi demo ii jibun wo shinjite

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
I don’t mind if we take a detour, 
as long as you believe in yourself.

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
Kitto motto sono saki he to

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
By doing that, I’m sure we can go even further.

02:18.640 --> 02:20.180
<b>What do you want me to do?</b>

02:36.370 --> 02:37.900
<b>No...</b>

02:37.900 --> 02:39.360
<b>Don’t leave me...</b>

02:45.940 --> 02:52.920
<b>What Vanished and What Was Born</b>

03:08.760 --> 03:09.760
<b>Huh?</b>

03:11.600 --> 03:13.430
<b>Good morning.</b>

03:13.430 --> 03:17.300
<b>I told you the other day to go to school, didn’t I?</b>

03:17.300 --> 03:18.540
<b>Yes.</b>

03:18.540 --> 03:20.640
<b>But I’m not here because I wanted to skip class...</b>

03:20.640 --> 03:24.410
<b>...or because I thought it’d be fun to be with you.</b>

03:24.410 --> 03:25.780
<b>That’s not why?</b>

03:25.780 --> 03:30.920
<b>I felt that I had something more important
than class to take care of right now.</b>

03:33.090 --> 03:35.020
<b>It involves the problem with prioritizing, you see.</b>

03:58.810 --> 04:00.750
<b>“Trust yourself.”</b>

04:04.150 --> 04:05.750
<b>Aren’t you going to have any?</b>

04:17.400 --> 04:19.300
<b>What’s wrong, boy?</b>

04:19.300 --> 04:21.530
<b>After making such a grand entrance
you’re starting to look pretty dull.</b>

04:30.580 --> 04:35.280
<b>Do you remember why I decided
to team up with you on this?</b>

04:35.280 --> 04:39.120
<b>You wanted to prove that the material
fairies really do exist, right?</b>

04:39.120 --> 04:39.850
<b>Yes.</b>

04:41.420 --> 04:43.320
<b>But I...</b>

04:43.920 --> 04:45.090
<b>But?</b>

04:45.720 --> 04:49.230
<b>At first, I didn’t care about these things
you could but couldn’t see...</b>

04:49.230 --> 04:53.300
<b>...or the true identities
of the material fairies.</b>

04:53.300 --> 04:56.770
<b>But then Rieko-chan asked me...</b>

04:56.770 --> 04:59.740
<b>“Have you ever seen something
you shouldn’t be able to see?”</b>

04:59.740 --> 05:04.210
<b>But a little later on, she told me she
didn’t care about them anymore...</b>

05:04.210 --> 05:06.610
<b>...and I didn’t understand why.</b>

05:06.610 --> 05:08.750
<b>So that’s why, huh?</b>

05:08.750 --> 05:11.800
<b>I’m pretty sure Rieko-chan never really cared about...</b>

05:11.800 --> 05:14.390
<b>...some strange things you could but couldn’t see.</b>

05:14.390 --> 05:17.420
<b>She probably just got a little bugged out knowing that Tanigawa and Kobayakawa...</b>

05:17.420 --> 05:20.830
<b>...had some secret that didn’t involve her.</b>

05:21.690 --> 05:27.330
<b>If Rieko-chan was keeping something
from me, I wouldn’t like it either.</b>

05:28.170 --> 05:29.670
<b>It would be difficult.</b>

05:32.640 --> 05:34.370
<b>I see now.</b>

05:34.370 --> 05:37.840
<b>Everyone was only focused on
chasing our own feelings...</b>

05:37.840 --> 05:40.850
<b>...and didn’t even bother trying to
meet eye to eye on anything.</b>

05:49.790 --> 05:53.120
<b>I wonder if our little alliance has reached its end?</b>

05:56.230 --> 06:00.400
<b>Even if you and I are searching for
the same thing, Sukawara-san...</b>

06:00.400 --> 06:02.900
<b>...I think what we’re both pursuing
in the end is different.</b>

06:05.070 --> 06:10.080
<b>But that’s because it’s obvious
that everyone is different...</b>

06:10.080 --> 06:11.880
<b>...and their thoughts
will also be different.</b>

06:11.880 --> 06:14.350
<b>Even if the exits they take
are different...</b>

06:15.550 --> 06:18.850
<b>It’s still possible to go
in the same direction.</b>

06:19.350 --> 06:22.250
<b>It is. I would still like
to do that with you.</b>

06:23.320 --> 06:24.790
<b>Why?</b>

06:24.790 --> 06:26.390
<b>Because I don’t want to run from this.</b>

06:33.170 --> 06:36.470
<b>I don’t want to run from these things
I’ve become involved with.</b>

06:36.470 --> 06:39.270
<b>If I run now, I think I’ll definitely regret it later.</b>

06:39.270 --> 06:41.410
<b>And I definitely don’t want that.</b>

06:45.040 --> 06:49.010
<b>I continue looking forward to working
with you on this, <i>Makabe-kun</i>.</b>

06:51.320 --> 06:52.220
<b>Yes!</b>

06:56.920 --> 06:59.860
<b>Now then, head off to school this minute.</b>

06:59.860 --> 07:00.690
<b>Eh?</b>

07:00.690 --> 07:03.030
<b>Not “Eh.”
“Yes, ma’am.”</b>

07:03.030 --> 07:05.400
<b>No way!</b>

07:10.040 --> 07:13.320
<b>So you’re always looking at this scene...</b>

07:13.320 --> 07:18.380
<b>Hey... I wonder why we saw those things anyway?</b>

07:18.380 --> 07:20.910
<b>What do you think about it?</b>

07:20.910 --> 07:22.050
<b>Not a clue.</b>

07:22.050 --> 07:25.080
<b>It was still before the whole thing
with the lights became popular.</b>

07:26.920 --> 07:30.490
<b>Sometimes I think maybe I was
chosen or something, but...</b>

07:30.490 --> 07:31.890
<b>That couldn’t be, huh?</b>

07:31.890 --> 07:34.890
<b>No. Actually, you might’ve been the one who chose.</b>

07:34.890 --> 07:38.130
<b>Excuse me?
I chose something?</b>

07:38.130 --> 07:40.060
<b>When? Why would I?</b>

07:41.070 --> 07:42.600
<b>Are you making fun of me?</b>

07:43.940 --> 07:46.300
<b>Keep looking at me, just like that.</b>

07:46.300 --> 07:47.240
<b>What is it?</b>

07:47.240 --> 07:49.540
<b>I want to draw you.</b>

07:49.540 --> 07:52.340
<b>Will you let me?</b>

08:07.090 --> 08:10.930
<b>Were you... some really amazing artist?</b>

08:10.930 --> 08:13.770
<b>I’m not sure about the “amazing” part...</b>

08:13.770 --> 08:16.900
<b>...but I’m a homeless artist right now.</b>

08:16.900 --> 08:18.900
<b>Even though you’re an artist, you’re homeless?</b>

08:18.900 --> 08:20.840
<b>I’m a homeless artist.</b>

08:20.840 --> 08:22.710
<b>There’s no paradox in that.</b>

08:22.710 --> 08:23.840
<b>But...</b>

08:23.840 --> 08:25.540
<b>You said it yourself, didn’t you?</b>

08:25.540 --> 08:28.610
<b>I was always looking at that scene.</b>

08:28.610 --> 08:29.880
<b>Yes... I did.</b>

08:29.880 --> 08:34.650
<b>I like picking up things that
have fallen into that scene.</b>

08:35.390 --> 08:39.160
<b>To continue doing that,
I always want to look at it.</b>

08:39.730 --> 08:42.030
<b>Does it have to be there?</b>

08:42.030 --> 08:44.230
<b>Rather than saying it’s a problem with the place...</b>

08:44.230 --> 08:46.460
<b>...I’d say it’s a problem with the way I decide to live.</b>

08:46.470 --> 08:47.670
<b>I don’t get you.</b>

08:48.700 --> 08:52.100
<b>The most comforting thing is not trying to look at it.</b>

08:52.100 --> 08:54.140
<b>So you’re particular about what you see.</b>

08:54.140 --> 08:55.540
<b>Because I’m an artist.</b>

08:55.540 --> 08:58.080
<b>But you’re not particular
in how you’re seen?</b>

08:58.080 --> 08:59.940
<b>Because I’m homeless.</b>

08:59.950 --> 09:03.150
<b>I think I’d be more interested
in wondering how I’m seen...</b>

09:03.750 --> 09:06.950
<b>People are always looking at how
they appear to other people, but...</b>

09:08.120 --> 09:14.390
<b>...no matter what the case, in the end,
people always see what they want to see.</b>

09:14.390 --> 09:15.730
<b>Wait a sec.</b>

09:15.730 --> 09:17.930
<b>When you said I was the one who chose,
is that what you meant?</b>

09:22.970 --> 09:24.070
<b>I’m done.</b>

09:30.210 --> 09:31.080
<b>Here.</b>

09:31.080 --> 09:32.180
<b>Thank you.</b>

09:38.780 --> 09:41.950
<b>So... this is how I look to you...</b>

09:41.950 --> 09:43.050
<b>That’s just a joke.</b>

09:43.060 --> 09:44.360
<b>Here.</b>

09:47.960 --> 09:49.530
<b>Is this some extra service?</b>

09:49.530 --> 09:51.400
<b>You drew it way too nicely...</b>

09:51.400 --> 09:52.860
<b>It’s as I saw you.</b>

09:52.860 --> 09:56.770
<b>The current you looks like this to me.</b>

09:58.040 --> 09:59.740
<b>Huh, Rieko?</b>

10:00.410 --> 10:01.510
<b>You’re right.</b>

10:01.510 --> 10:03.810
<b>Rieko, what happened to school?</b>

10:04.910 --> 10:06.680
<b>I should be asking you two that.</b>

10:06.680 --> 10:08.550
<b>What were you doing?</b>

10:08.550 --> 10:11.920
<b>Did you get a bad grade on a test,
so you got away to have some fun?</b>

10:11.920 --> 10:14.120
<b>Well, a few things pulled me away.</b>

10:14.120 --> 10:15.450
<b>Like what?</b>

10:15.450 --> 10:17.160
<b>A little thing I have going with this guy.</b>

10:17.160 --> 10:19.560
<b>Wait a sec! Rieko!</b>

10:19.560 --> 10:21.560
<b>Did she just say a “guy”?</b>

10:21.560 --> 10:23.030
<b>Rieko got herself a boyfriend?</b>

